        "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola by Completing the Square",
        "problem": "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3{x}^{2}-30x-8y+67=0.$",
        "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-30x-8y+67 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-30x & =8y-67 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-10x] & =8y-67 \\\\ 3[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =8y-67 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2}-75 & =8y-67 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2} & =8y-67+75 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2} & =8y+8 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2} & =8(y+1) \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =\\frac{8}{3}(y+1) \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =4(\\frac{2}{3})(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(5,-1).$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
