        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Asymptotes of a Hyperbola Given Its Equation in Non-Standard Form",
        "problem": "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $8{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}=200.$",
        "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $200$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =200 \\\\ \\frac{8{y}^{2}}{200}-\\frac{25{x}^{2}}{200} & =\\frac{200}{200} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{25}=5,$ and $b=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{2}}x=\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{4}x.$",
